a parenthesised sub-expression must not inherit a pending dereference.

DEREFERENCING THE RESULT OF A CONDITIONAL SEGFAULTED, and the star landed on
the CONDITION:

    v = *(1 ? p1 : p2);

    mov_rax, %1                  # the condition, the literal 1
    movsx_rax,DWORD_PTR_[rax]    # THE STAR, applied to 1 as an address
    # TERNARY_main_0
    test_rax,rax                 # and the garbage load became the condition
    ...
    movsx_rax,DWORD_PTR_[rax]    # the real dereference, emitted correctly

Two loads for one star. The second is right; the first reads address 1.

THIS IS EXACTLY function_call's ARGUMENT-LIST HAZARD, ONE DOOR OVER, and that
function already carries the fix and the reasoning: "A pending `*` is parked in
num_dereference_after_postfix when the stars are eaten, for the postfix walk to
apply once the chain is resolved... The count belongs to the expression that
parked it, never to a sub-expression." Its worked example is `*give(8)`, where
the star landed on the literal 8 -- the same two lines of M1, the same wrong
operand, a different pair of brackets.

A parenthesised expression is a separate expression context for the same
reason an argument list is: it is parsed BETWEEN the star being eaten and the
postfix walk that consumes the count, and everything inside reads the same
global. The ternary is simply the most visible way in, because its CONDITION
is parsed before `?` is seen -- so the stray load is already emitted by the
time anything knows a ternary is being parsed, and no edit to the ternary
handler can reach it.

WHERE tcc WRITES IT. tccgen.c:2939, inside combine_types:

    type = *(bt1 == VT_PTR ? type1 : type2);

combine_types decides the type of every binary operator and every conditional
in the program being compiled, so this is on the path of essentially every
expression tcc parses.

THE BOUNDARY IS THE PARENTHESES, NOT SOMETHING LARGER. EXPERIMENT-zzzg
restored this same count around a whole call rather than around the argument
list and took mc-tcc from 12/12 to 0/12. The region that must not see the
count is the sub-expression itself and nothing more, so the save/clear/restore
brackets comma_expression() alone and sits inside the existing
assign_through_parens save/restore rather than replacing it.

It is also why the local count is untouched: the `*(` path in the dereference
handler counts its stars in a LOCAL num_dereference and applies them after
primary_expr returns, so `*(p)` still dereferences p exactly as before. Only
the global that sub-expressions can see is cleared.

MEASURED, EITHER SIDE (vendored pin + full series):

    difftest amd64      103 pass, 0 fail, 2 known gaps   (116 closed)
    difftest aarch64    104 pass, 0 fail, 2 known gaps   (116 closed)
    case 116            SIGSEGV -> 0, all five probes
    case 113            passes                            unchanged
    case 22  ternary in an arglist   passes               unchanged
    case 105 dereferenced call result passes              unchanged

The three neighbouring cases are named because they are what a wrong version
of this breaks: 22 is a ternary inside an argument list, where both this
bracket and function_call's are live at once; 105 is the `*give(8)` shape
itself; 113 is the conditional's type.

--- a/cc_core.c
+++ b/cc_core.c
@@ -4221,9 +4221,29 @@ void primary_expr(void)
 				 * branch twice: the outer parenthesis sees the `+=` and sets
 				 * the flag, and the inner one sees only a `)` after itself
 				 * and would clear it again -- leaving the variable loaded and
 				 * the store writing through its value. Saving and restoring
 				 * is the same shape Address_of uses four lines up. */
 				int saved_atp = assign_through_parens;
 				assign_through_parens = assign_after_parens || saved_atp;
+				/* AND A PENDING `*` BELONGS TO US, NOT TO WHAT IS INSIDE.
+				 *
+				 * num_dereference_after_postfix parks a star that has been
+				 * eaten but not yet applied. Everything parsed in here is a
+				 * sub-expression that reads the same global, so in
+				 *     v = *(1 ? p1 : p2)
+				 * the star landed on the CONDITION and loaded address 1.
+				 *
+				 * Identical to the argument-list hazard function_call
+				 * documents at the top of this file -- `*give(8)`, the same
+				 * two lines of M1, a different pair of brackets. The ternary
+				 * is the loudest way in because its condition is parsed
+				 * before `?` is seen, so no edit to the ternary handler can
+				 * reach it.
+				 *
+				 * comma_expression() ALONE, deliberately: zzzg widened this
+				 * same restore to a whole call and cost 12/12 -> 0/12. */
+				int paren_pending_deref = num_dereference_after_postfix;
+				num_dereference_after_postfix = 0;
 				comma_expression();
+				num_dereference_after_postfix = paren_pending_deref;
 				assign_through_parens = saved_atp;
